      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-21T10:13:58Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): write waterjet header notes as one clean comment\n\nMain's #2996 header notes reach every shipped post through onComment.\nThe waterjet post had none, so the PRELUDE default wrote a note raw: a\nhostile model name could put live words on the line. The post now\nwrites the note as one parenthesis comment through commentText, like\nthe plasma and wire posts. The shipped-post walk now counts 20 posts\nand gives the waterjet post a waterjet machine.\n\nPinned by header_notes_use_each_shipped_dialect_and_keep_the_full_surface_bound.\n\nRefs #1882\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
